  public_claim: tiny fixture local generation is verified for f32, q8_0, q4_0, a custom BPE f32 fixture whose runtime diagnostics prove prompt the merges to tokenizer output 256,261, and a tied-output f32 fixture that omits output.weight only under the v1 tied-output flag; TinyLM-16M f32, q8_0, and q4_0 deterministic smoke generation are verified; core math now has direct tests for dot, matvec, matmul, RMSNorm, softmax, SiLU, SwiGLU, and shape failures; .slm checksum generation, mismatch rejection, native admission validation, eight provenance manifests, runtime-smoke quality gating, assistant-quality rejection for pending eval templates, raw-f32 trained-source validation, converted-trained source conversion for f32/q8_0/q4_0, and fixture-scoped native eval sidecar generation for f32/q8_0/q4_0 are verified; assistant-quality evidence gates require positive eval case totals, zero failed cases, and exact per-case expected/actual matches while rejecting zero-case files, stray case keys, and missing case evidence; q8_0 and q4_0 matrix dispatch use direct quantized matvec and no longer keep full decoded f32 shadow tensors; model loading pre-resolves top-level and per-layer tensor indices, the token loop no longer formats layer tensor names, and tied-output projection flags route logits through token embeddings; runtime generation reuses model-loaded scratch/logits across prompt generation and step-token calls, top-k diagnostics do not allocate a vocab-sized candidate vector, stochastic sampling uses fixed 1024-candidate buffers, accepts BPE top_k 262, and rejects oversized top-k without a vocab-sized candidate vector; context-boundary generation accepts the last prompt slot and rejects full-context prompts with clean diagnostics, and successful generation extends token state for step-token continuation; the browser UI keeps a local User/TinyRustLM conversation transcript with Clear separate from runtime Reset and smoke-tested desktop/mobile Clear-click behavior; the WASM ABI returns explicit ErrorCode values for generate_next_token, exposes stepped token text through last_result and selected token through diagnostics, verifies free_model, and rejects post-free generation as ModelNotLoaded; the no-crate Rust local server serves app/WASM/model/manifest routes and Visual Studio F5 reuses verified Rust-hosted servers; the no-crate Rust mini browser harness verifies static app contract, Rust WASM export definitions, and loopback route content types; browser reload/reset/model-switch, missing-model, malformed-model, context-overflow, desktop/mobile UI audit with visible local model provenance, endurance, WASM ABI invalid-boundary, benchmark-panel performance smoke and performance soak, and Visual Studio busy-port fallback coverage are verified; do not claim product trained-model quality yet.
